Tonight's qemu-ga ping gap was a SYMPTOM of VM 1010 being starved
(CPU/memory/IO), not the cause. Different failure mode from previous
documented occurrences of TS-K8S-038. The doc's occurrences #1-3 had
captured evidence of actual busy loop; occurrence #4 (tonight) does not.

### Recommendation:
Update TS-K8S-038 doc to note this distinction. Future occurrences
should capture strace early to distinguish between:
- Real TS-K8S-038: qemu-ga at 98% CPU, strace shows EAGAIN loop
- Tonight's mode: qemu-ga at low CPU, ping gap from scheduling starvation

