[Lessons Learned]

## On the investigation process

1. Symptom correlation is NOT causation
   - logind bursts coincided with IO spikes → incorrectly assumed cause
   - sssd restart coincided with cascade → incorrectly assumed cause
   - In both cases, the "correlation" was shared downstream effect

2. Confidence should scale inversely with ease of theory generation
   - Each theory fit the evidence at the time it was proposed
   - Each theory was wrong
   - Multiple plausible theories = probably need more evidence, not
     commitment to one

3. User intuition matters
   - User pushed back with "I'm not convinced" multiple times
   - Each pushback led to new evidence that disproved current theory
   - "Why only sometimes when it runs all day?" was the right question
     about Prometheus

4. Simple answers deserve consideration early
   - "Prod works, dev doesn't, prod has more resources" was the answer
     from the start
   - Spent hours on exotic theories before returning to resources

5. Boot storms and normal-operation events are different phenomena
   - Both show as spikes on PSI graph
   - Need different analysis approaches
   - Should not be lumped together when evaluating fixes

## On the technical environment

6. PSI metrics need context to interpret
   - "Some" vs "Full" meaning differ significantly
   - High "Some" can be normal under bursty workloads
   - High "Full" means literally everything is blocked — much worse

7. iostat cumulative average is misleading
   - First iostat output is average since boot
   - Includes past anomalies in the average
   - Always need 2-3 live samples to see current state

8. etcd is fragile on shared storage with small VM RAM
   - bbolt mmap depends heavily on page cache
   - When page cache thrashes, every read hits disk
   - 3 etcd instances on one NVMe + small RAM = fragility

9. Liveness probes assume fast apiserver
   - Most default probes use 1s timeout
   - Cluster under stress → apiserver slow → probes fail → cascade
   - Custom timeouts are critical in resource-constrained environments

10. "It works in prod" is a feature, not a bug
    - Prod config working means the problem is environmental, not
      software
    - The fix is to make dev match prod or accept reduced expectations

