[Investigator Notes]

This investigation is messy on purpose. I'm leaving in the wrong
theories because:

1. Future me reading this should see how the investigation actually
   went — not a sanitized "here's the answer" doc
2. The wrong theories had evidence that looked compelling. Same
   evidence might come up again — worth remembering why it was
   not the answer
3. The trail of reversals is a teaching case: this is what happens
   when you have an underprovisioned system with many interacting
   components. Single-root-cause thinking fails.

The useful framing might be: "pve-dev is a complex system operating
near its resource limits. It fails in random ways that all look
similar on the PSI graph. Different failures at different times have
different triggers but similar symptoms. No single fix will eliminate
spikes while the underlying resource constraint exists."

Honest summary: tonight I was confidently wrong multiple times.
I apologize for sending you down rabbit holes. The real answer was
always visible ("dev has less resources than prod which works fine")
but I kept chasing interesting-looking evidence instead of trusting
the simple comparison.

Going forward: when you see a PSI spike tomorrow, the first question
should be "did anything change?" (reboot, deploy, backup). If no →
investigate via TS-K8S-038 playbook (capture strace early). If yes →
likely boot/rejoin storm, wait 5 minutes, move on.

